      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Base rate/reference class: for a normal recent CDFI Fund assistance-award year, the fetched FY2024 announced award components sum to 712.7 million = 408.2 CDFI/NACA FA + 246.4 CMF + 40.1 BEA + 18.0 SDL. This is a proxy for the registered USAspending transaction-obligation target; Capital Magnet Fund inclusion under the CDFI awarding-subagency and financial-assistance query is a material uncertainty. The pandemic ERP year is not used as the central prior because its 1.73 billion ERP award was a one-off emergency program rather than a repeatable FY2026 mechanism."
      },
      {
        "kind": "math",
        "text": "Model candidates under thesis_model_candidate_v1: persistence candidate point 712.7, p10 340, p50 712.7, p90 910, 80% interval 340-910, 90% interval 250-1000, interval_method recent-award empirical proxy, calibration_n 3, train_cutoff FY2025 partial, walk_forward_score unavailable; appropriation-anchor candidate point 324.0, p10 260, p50 324, p90 713, 80% interval 260-713, 90% interval 200-900, interval_method appropriation-plus-cycle dispersion proxy, calibration_n 3, train_cutoff FY2026 enacted text, walk_forward_score unavailable. I select a shrinkage blend because the FY2026 enacted account is level at 324 but award timing is disrupted and the target captures transaction obligations, including carryover-funded awards."
      },
      {
        "kind": "math",
        "text": "Prior/update/interval: prior = FY2024 normal-cycle award-announcement proxy persistence 712.7; historical sample = [712.7 FY2024 announced award proxy, 348.0 FY2025 planned round, 324.0 FY2026 enacted account]; adjustment components = 65% persistence weight and 35% current appropriation weight plus +10 for likely catch-up/rounding from delayed FY2025/2026 awards; point = 0.65*712.7 + 0.35*324.0 + 10 = 586.3, rounded to 590. For the interval, sigma = 218 from the proxy sample values; 1.28*sigma = 279, rounded to about 270 to nearest $10 million. This is proxy uncertainty, not realized same-query target volatility, but it is intentionally wide for source-mapping and transaction-timing risk. Implied 80% bounds: 590 - 270 = 320 and 590 + 270 = 860."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Downside risk: the outcome would land below the interval if FY2025 FA/TA catch-up awards are not obligated by September 30, 2026, if USAspending records most FY2026 award agreements after the fiscal year closes, if Capital Magnet Fund obligations do not appear in the registered CDFI awarding-subagency query, or if compliance-review changes materially reduce award execution. Upside risk: it would land above the interval if delayed FY2025 awards, FY2026 BEA/SDL awards, and a large Capital Magnet Fund round all post as FY2026 CDFI Fund financial-assistance transactions."
      },
